.TH tubase32 n 0.2 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tubase32
.PP
RFC 4648 base32 (and base32hex) encode/decode in pure Tcl. Tcl core provides base64 but not base32, so this fills the gap with a matching API.
.SS API
.CS
set b32  [::tclutils::tubase32::encode $bytes]
set data [::tclutils::tubase32::decode $b32]
.CE
.PP
Commands:
.IP \(bu
\fBencode data ?\-pad bool? ?\-hex bool?\fR — base32 string. \fB\-pad 0\fR omits the trailing \fB=\fR; \fB\-hex 1\fR uses the base32hex alphabet (RFC 4648 §7). Default \fB\-pad 1 \-hex 0\fR.
.IP \(bu
\fBdecode text ?\-hex bool?\fR — back to a binary string. Whitespace and \fB=\fR padding are ignored; input is case\-insensitive. The tail is checked as in RFC 4648 §3.5: the number of data characters must be one \fBencode\fR produces (a multiple of 8 plus 0, 2, 4, 5 or 7), and the bits left after the last whole byte must be zero. \fBdecode MY\fR is \fBf\fR; \fBdecode MZ\fR is an error.
.IP \(bu
\fBencodeFile path ?\-pad bool? ?\-hex bool?\fR — encode a file's bytes.
.IP \(bu
\fBdecodeFile path ?\-hex bool?\fR — decode a file's text.
.PP
Unlike \fBtclutils::tubase64::decode\fR (which returns an empty string for text that is not base64), invalid base32 raises an error:
.TS
l l.
Error code	When
\fB{TCLUTILS TUBASE32 CHAR}\fR	a character outside the alphabet
\fB{TCLUTILS TUBASE32 LENGTH}\fR	1, 3 or 6 data characters in the last group
\fB{TCLUTILS TUBASE32 BITS}\fR	non\-zero bits after the last byte
\fB{TCLUTILS COMMON BOOLEAN \-pad}\fR / \fB\-hex\fR	option value not a boolean
.TE
